Self (archive footage), played by John Hinckley Jr..

7
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Faces of Death (later re-released as The Original Faces of Death) is a 1978 American mondo horror film written and
directed by John Alan Schwartz, credited under the pseudonyms "Conan Le Cilaire" and "Alan Black" respectively.

8
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:42,000
The film, presented as if it were an actual
documentary, centers on pathologist Francis B.

9
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:54,000
Gröss, played by actor Michael Carr, who presents the viewer with footage
showing different gruesome ways of dying from a variety of sources.

10
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Many scenes were faked for the film, but most portions include
pre-existing video footage of real deaths and its aftermath.

11
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:18,000
Faces of Death received generally negative reviews, but it was a huge success at
the box office, reportedly grossing over $35 million worldwide.

12
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
It gained a cult following and spawned several sequels, the first
of which, Faces of Death II, was released in 1981.

13
01:07:36,000 --> 01:07:42,000
The film explores themes of necrophilia, gore, car
accident, fake documentary, mortuary.

14
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
The tone is dark.
